{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-1","title":"John 7:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jesus reproves the ambition and boldness of his kinsmen; 10 goes up from Galilee to the feast of tabernacles; 14 teaches in the temple. 40 Divers opinions of him among the people. 45 The Pharisees are angry that their officers took him not, and chide with Nicodemus for taking his part.</p>\n<p>A.M. 4037. A.D. 33. walked. 4:3,54; 10:39,40; 11:54; Lu 13:31-33; Ac 10:38 Jewry.Jewry, or Judea, as distinguished from Galilee and Samaria, contained the tribes of Judah, Benjamin, Simeon, and Dan, being bounded on the north by the village Annach or Dorceus, on the borders of Samaria; on the south by a village called Jarda in Arabia; and extending in breadth from the river Jordan to Joppa and the Mediterranean, having Jerusalem in its centre.</p>\n<p>because. 19,25; 5:16-18; Mt 10:23; 21:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-2","title":"John 7:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Ex 23:16,17; Le 23:34-43; Nu 29:12-38; De 16:13-16; 1Ki 8:2,65 2Ch 7:9,10; Ezr 3:4; Ne 8:14-18; Zec 14:16-19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-3","title":"John 7:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>brethren. 5; Mt 12:46,47; Mr 3:31; Lu 8:19; Ac 2:14 Depart. Ge 37:5-11,20; 1Sa 17:28; Jer 12:6; Mt 22:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-4","title":"John 7:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>there. Pr 18:1,2; Mt 6:1,2,5,16; 23:5; Lu 6:45 shew. 18:20; 1Ki 22:13; Mt 4:6; Ac 2:4-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-5","title":"John 7:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p