p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-20","title":"John 7:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Thou. 8:48,52; 10:20; Mt 10:25; 11:18,19; 12:24; Mr 3:21,22,30; Ac 26:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-21","title":"John 7:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>I have. 5:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-22","title":"John 7:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>circumcision. Ge 17:10-14; Le 12:3; Ro 4:9-11; Ga 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-23","title":"John 7:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>that the law of Moses should not be broken. or, withoutbreaking the law of Moses. Mt 12:5 I have made.Rather, \"I have healed a whole man\" [holos anthropos ,] and not the circumcised member only. This reasoning was in perfect accordance with the principles of the Jews. So Tanchuma, \"Circumcision, which is performed on one of the 248 members of man, vacates the sabbath; how much more the whole body of a man!\"</p>\n<p>5:8,9,14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-24","title":"John 7:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>8:15; De 1:16,17; 16:18,19; Ps 58:1,2; 82:2; 94:20,21; Pr 17:15 Pr 24:23; Isa 5:23; 11:3,4; Jas 2:1,4,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-25","title":"John 7:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>of Jerusalem. 10,11 Is not. 20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-26","title":"John 7:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>he speaketh. Ps 40:9,10; 71:15,16; Pr 28:1; Isa 42:4; 50:7,8; Mt 22:16; Ac 4:13 Eph 6:19,20; Php 1:14; 2Ti 1:7,8 Do. 48; 9:22; 11:47-53; 12:42; Lu 7:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-27","title":"John 7:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>we know. 15; 6:42; Mt 13:54-57; Mr 6:3; Lu 4:22 no man. 41,42; Isa 11:1; 53:8; Jer 23:5; 30:21; Mic 5:2; Mt 2:5,6; Ac 8:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-28","title":"John 7:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Ye both. 1:46; 8:14; Mt 2:23; Lu 2:4,11,39,51 and I. 3:2; 5:43; 8:16,42; 10:36; 12:49; 14:10,31 is true. 3:33; 5:32; 8:26; Ro 3:4; 2Co 1:18; Tit 1:2; Heb 6:18; 1Jo 5:10 whom. 8:19,54,55; 16:3; 17:3,25; 1Sa 2:12; Ps 9:10; Pr 2:3-5; Jer 9:6 Jer 31:34; Ho 4:1; 5:4; 6:3-6; Mt 11:27; Lu 10:22; Ac 17:23; Ro 1:28 2Co 4:6; 1Jo 2:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-29","title":"John 7:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>I. 1:18; 8:55; 10:15; 17:25,26 for. 3:16,17; 13:3; 16:27,28; 17:18; 1Jo 1:2; 4:9,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-30","title":"John 7:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>they. 19,32; 8:37,59; 10:31,39; 11:57; Mr 11:18; Lu 19:47,48; 20:19 but. 6,8,44-46; 8:20; 9:4; 11:9,10; Ps 76:10; Isa 46:10; Lu 13:32,33 Lu 22:53</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-31","title":"John 7:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>believed. 2:23,24; 4:39; 6:14,15; 8:30-32; 12:42; Mt 12:23; Lu 8:13; Ac 8:13 Jas 2:26 When. 3:2; 6:2; 9:16; 10:41,42; Mt 11:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-7-32","title":"John 7:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":7,"verseSta